# Security

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 6 — Engineering

## Purpose

Documents how GrantAI enforces its governance rules (Tier 3/4 restrictions
from `GOVERNANCE.md`) as actual technical controls, not just process
convention.

## Principles

1. **Tier boundaries are enforced in the database, not just in agent
   prompts.** An agent "knowing" it shouldn't submit an application is not
   sufficient — row-level security policies on `applications.submitted_date`
   and `funding_organizations.status` make it structurally impossible for
   the service-role credential to write those fields, per
   `DatabaseSchema.md`.
2. **Separate credentials for separate trust levels.** Service-role key
   (agents, scheduled jobs) vs. founder session auth (frontend, human
   actions) are never the same credential — see `API.md`.
3. **No credentials in agent context.** Per the existing Anthropic-API
   pattern used across BAE apps, API keys are never passed into the agent
   prompt/context; they're handled at the request layer.

## Data Sensitivity

- Business profile data (`business_profiles` table) is internal financial
  information about the business(es) GrantAI serves — treat with the same
  care as any other financial data in the BAE portfolio, restricted to
  founder-authenticated access
- Grant application drafts may contain sensitive business detail before
  they're ever submitted — draft content should not be publicly readable
  even if other parts of the app are

## Source Sweep Safety

Grant Hunter reaches out to external funding-source websites/APIs on a
schedule. Standard web-scraping/API-hygiene practices apply: respect
rate limits and terms of service for each source in
`FundingOrganizations.md`, and treat a source blocking or rate-limiting
Hunter as a failure to surface in the run digest (`AuditLogging.md`), not
something to route around.

